<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n405" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accŭbĭtus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m., = accubitio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A reclining at table</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Ach.
				1, 110</span></i> (quoted by <i><span class="en">Prisc.
			863</span></i> P.); <i><span class="en">id. Theb. 1, 714</span></i>; and
			perh. also Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 20, 11,
			19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Per meton., <i>a couch</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Cant.
				1, 11</span></i>; <i>a place on a couch</i>, <i><span class="en">ib. Luc. 14,
				7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
